{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing","id":13377,"title":"Demon got free healing?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-18T07:17:01-08:00","id":13377,"title":"Demon got free healing?","content":"I wasn't big fan of the old world of darkness - but then came new world of darkness. I was impressed - one thing that i really loved ( and hated lack of it in the ascension ) was one simply uwritten rule - no free healing. And then demon came and destroyed my dreams of system clean of this game breaking thing - its called on the mend. It's not only crazy powerful, but it also break things already estabilished in the book. As far i understand embeds are simple intuitive abilities, that look pretty concidental and exploits are powerful more out of this world abilities that are coming from powering up a lot the embeds. We do have really nice exploit - Break to Heal. Why it works is perfectly layed out with nice philosophy, it is costly as every other exploit - point of aether and compromise roll. And its great. But if we look like on the mend - its not weaker than break to heal! Yes we do have weaker exploit than embed , embed that cost nothing and even heals aggravated wounds! And why it's doing it? Because destroyers are masters of destroying things and can reverse it to heal... It have no sense. Regrow instantly a hand that was nuked off by mage by erasing it from reality is in fact REALLY supernatural. And having someone with this ability and 7 dice means that demons will get always fully healed after a battle which in my opinion kills all this paranoia feeling that this game i thought should be about. I really do hope this is just a draft and it can still be changed - if it's not - sorry but i am out. I do have a lot of core books of new world of darkness sitting on my shelf - i was really happy when i read god machine chronicle i really thought that there is a really nice new quality to the new polished system and all that is after that will be glorious. But now... All what i see is old world of darkness happening again - and its a sad day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1194,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1194-soul31","user":"soul31","date":". 11-18-2013, 10:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1194-soul31","name":"soul31","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T07:35:16-08:00","id":13386,"title":"","content":"Looking at Break to Heal versus On the Mend, it does seem like there is no good reason to use Break to Heal if On the Mend is available.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T07:36:13-08:00","id":13388,"title":"","content":"So... you don't like ONE (1) power and... you are ditching a whole game for that. And claiming all gamelines are ruined forever from this point on. Yeah, pretty sensible reaction you had there.<br /> <br /> EDIT: specially since this being a world of darkness game you could just ignore that particular power (or tweak it to your liking) and be done with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". 11-18-2013, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T07:47:56-08:00","id":13390,"title":"","content":"I have to agree, On the Mend seems to be broken and doesn't really fit as an embed. Its only weakness is that it requires an instant action instead of being reflexive. I'm hoping that the 1% missing in the preview PDF contains an improved version of this power. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Actually I don't think a healing embed is really needed. There are some nice damage avoidance embeds that allow a demon to survive a combat without feeling overpowered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T07:57:33-08:00","id":13394,"title":"","content":"I like there being healing embeds, and I certainly don't have problems with cheap/free healing, but it could stand to be a less superior option, or Break to Heal needs to step up.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T08:33:13-08:00","id":13405,"title":"","content":"Yes thats true i don`t like one power - but this is first game in the line and this one power break the rule that was estabilished in nwod - one rule that i loved. If we got something like this in the first line of new god machine world of darkness system i dread what is coming next. Also there are others embeds that people don't like and talk about in other threads it's not one power problem - it's does anyone playtested it? - kind of problem. Game looks great conceptually but if we start looking on some powers... It doesn't look good - it doesn't look &quot;new world of darkness&quot; quality as i like to call it. And when i said it i meant powers that are adding something to the game and not just put there because someone put the there because he thinks they're cool(flying werewolfs like comets cough cough). Look on werewolf forsaken gift list in core book - all of them are oozing with werewolfness, i do really feel like werewolf when i used them. In demon we do have some great ones but there are still few that are - gamebreaking. And a power that destroys everything that is estabilished about what embeds are and what exploits are and how they work? This is one power - but because of it i got into a big fight because i let my players think about all embeds and one of them looked on fringe teories and such to create one(it was about morphogenetic field) and other gave me this is so damn supernatural power - i asked him why and he pointed me to this one on the mend and said - i am destroyer so i am master of both creation and destruction, so if i can easily heal aggravated damage i shouldn't have any problem of creating weapons out of my bones (assasin creed style) or using bones of the others to do a instant kills(making bone grow to kill from inside). I was speechless... Because logically his argument is sound and because this ONE power exist it is supported by authors of the system...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1194-soul31","name":"soul31","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T08:34:55-08:00","id":13407,"title":"","content":"Look. I haven't read these two powers extensively enough to judge, but &quot;On the Mend is overpowered as an Embed when comparing to the more expensive and less effective Break to Heal Exploit&quot;. I can't judge the validity of the statement, but it's a statement that will make sense.<br /> <br /> However, &quot;On the Mend is more powerful than Break to Heal in the <i>preview</i> of the text, and as a consequence [i]the entirety of Demon: the Descent and by extension the entirety of ten years of NWoD is completely irrepairably broken and all is lost&quot;, is... About as nonsensical as a statement can ever be. You might want to revisit the scale of this problem and adjust your outrage accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T08:36:07-08:00","id":13408,"title":"","content":"&quot;Actually I don't think a healing embed is really needed. There are some nice damage avoidance embeds that allow a demon to survive a combat without feeling overpowered. &quot;<br /> That is not so in my eyes, as EVERY splat has some healing powers.<br /> <br /> For on the mend: Yes it is powerful. (Except for the aggrevated damage healing it is around as effective as werewolf healing when you use essence to enhance it...with aggrevated it is even more powerful).<br /> <br /> A few possibilities exist there: a.) making it an exploit b.) making it cost 1 aether each c.) Making it so that it only can be used primum times during a specific time period and each use afterwards creates a compromise roll.<br /> <br /> Personally I think c is the best solution as there are already embeds who use that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T08:58:45-08:00","id":13419,"title":"","content":"Making it cost an Aether would break the &quot;Embeds don't cost Aether&quot; rule.<br /> <br /> I'd just delete it rather than make it an Exploit - we have Break to Heal, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T08:59:05-08:00","id":13420,"title":"","content":"Who said that &quot;no free healing&quot; was a hard-and-fast rule of NWoD? Must've missed that memo. <br /> <br /> But: I've gotten a couple of comments about On the Mend, and it might bear a rethink. I will say, though, that I <i>hate</i> arbitrary limits on powers done in the name of &quot;balance.&quot; There are a lot of Embeds that do have limits on how often they can be used or how (and whether) they attract angelic attention, but none of that is in service to &quot;balance&quot;, it's in service to the setting being consistent. <br /> <br /> The comparison to Break to Heal is a fair point, though. Will noodle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T09:18:44-08:00","id":13432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=13420#post13420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said that &quot;no free healing&quot; was a hard-and-fast rule of NWoD? Must've missed that memo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that &quot;free healing&quot; is in the <i>core WoD book</i> as a baseline feature (everyone healing damage over time with no expenditure unless otherwise stated), I'm not sure what memo the OP got, because clearly <i>noone else ever did</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T09:32:30-08:00","id":13441,"title":"","content":"What about this: &quot;The target heals at an acceleraterated rate for a number of hours equal to the demons successes. Recovering one bashing per minute, one lethal every half hour, and one aggravated level every three hours.&quot; That keeps the Embed useful, and true to its original purpose without raining on Break to Heal's parade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 11-18-2013, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T09:50:28-08:00","id":13453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=13420#post13420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said that &quot;no free healing&quot; was a hard-and-fast rule of NWoD? Must've missed that memo.<br /> <br /> But: I've gotten a couple of comments about On the Mend, and it might bear a rethink. I will say, though, that I <i>hate</i> arbitrary limits on powers done in the name of &quot;balance.&quot; There are a lot of Embeds that do have limits on how often they can be used or how (and whether) they attract angelic attention, but none of that is in service to &quot;balance&quot;, it's in service to the setting being consistent.<br /> <br /> The comparison to Break to Heal is a fair point, though. Will noodle.</div> </div> </div> </div>A compromise could be a slight restriction like a few embeds already have. As examples:<br /> just bruised has -1 on each roll regardless of success/failure for a scene, fungible knowledge can be used resolve times per day without causing a compromise roll as examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":914,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","user":"Ryu","date":". 11-18-2013, 12:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T10:01:54-08:00","id":13462,"title":"","content":"As i said this was like unwritten rule - propably there wasn't any memo or anything - maybe it just happened to be that the even mages who are masters of reality are paying for even covert self healing. They pay for &quot; significantly altering the laws of nature or physics&quot; in other word doing some supernatural like hell things like you know instantly healing aggravated damage? Propably you are right, there wasn't any rule but this happened to be that way and it worked so why suddenly change it? You maked your demons vulnerable as humans and then you gave them option for instant free healing - it's weird to be honest. Ok maybe you as a author wanted demons to seem vulnerable and weak and don't really be? So why just bruised got -1 ever use and this one don't? It doesn't have any sense... On the mend is more even more powerful that just bruised and everyone seem complaining about that power... And it clearly blurrs a division what embed can do before its called an exploit... To be honest i would like to hear some argumentation why this power is even there. Maybe i am missing something. I lost all my players because the argument i got because of this power. Propably i over reacted - sorry. I just wanted to be heard before the game goes to print with rule like that - if it can be changed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1194-soul31","name":"soul31","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T10:04:34-08:00","id":13466,"title":"","content":"@soul if you talk about free self healing.....there is only 1 thing that never got one before that was aggrevated.......werewolfes could heal bashing and lethal quite good without any costs involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":914,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","user":"Ryu","date":". 11-18-2013, 01:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T10:12:52-08:00","id":13473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=13420#post13420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I <i>hate</i> arbitrary limits on powers done in the name of &quot;balance.&quot; There are a lot of Embeds that do have limits on how often they can be used or how (and whether) they attract angelic attention, but none of that is in service to &quot;balance&quot;, it's in service to the setting being consistent.<br /> <br /> The comparison to Break to Heal is a fair point, though. Will noodle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe in balance, specifically when we have a good apples-to-apples comparison like in this case, but senseless limits are not the way to go about it and I greatly appreciate that attitude from you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T10:58:46-08:00","id":13498,"title":"","content":"@Ryu what gift or other werewolf power you're mentioning?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1194-soul31","name":"soul31","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T11:10:56-08:00","id":13503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>soul31</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=13498#post13498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Ryu what gift or other werewolf power you're mentioning?</div> </div> </div> </div>no gift (they got a healing gift though), it is their intrinsic healing power I meant: 1 bashing per turn, 1 lethal per 15 mins (they can enhance it to 1+ lethal per turn by spending essence, but the 1 bashing/turn, 1 lethal/15 mins is absolutely cost free with not a single drawback, thus I count that as free healing).<br /> <br /> I count it as &quot;power&quot; in this sense though as it is (an absolutely cost free ... even xp free) advantage they have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T12:00:17-08:00","id":13530,"title":"","content":"It's not the same - it still slows them down - just a bit less. If someone in the pack is wounded (and don't want to spend essence) for let's say 4 lethal ( which in gmc rules is very propable) the pack still need to wait 1 hour for their brother or sister to fully recover. What about demon cell with someone having on the mend? Around 12 seconds for wounded person and group is ready to go... Let me use more concise wording i meant free instant healing. Or even more precise - free instant aggravated and/or lethal wounds healing. There may be some power that i don't know that heals bashing damage that is free and it's fine. But as on the mend is - it's everyone should have kind of embed now...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1194,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1194-soul31","user":"soul31","date":". 11-18-2013, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1194-soul31","name":"soul31","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T12:01:49-08:00","id":13534,"title":"","content":"This may be a change in the wind indicating that nWoD is going to change direction towards more cheap healing. Personally I welcome it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T12:16:23-08:00","id":13539,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking about other examples of healing powers that are instant actions and heal agg that exist across the other game lines. True most of them cost a supernatural resource, but those that do can be more powerful then On the Mend. <br /> <br /> Mages can heal anything but agg damage for free with 2 dots in the Life arcanum. Its not even vulgar as long as they make at least a small effort to make the healing look normal. <br /> <br /> Prometheans heal pretty much an unlimited amount of any type of damage as long as they have access to electricity (because that is so rare in the modern world =P)<br /> <br /> Geist lets you (as part of the Template) negate damage including Agg damage as a 1:1 ratio. <br /> <br /> Mummy's heal one point of bashing per round. For a single point of their supernatural resource they heal 1 lethal and 3 bashing a round for the rest of a scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T12:19:20-08:00","id":13540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=13539#post13539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geist lets you (as part of the Template) negate damage including Agg damage as a 1:1 ratio.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that, but when it does come back (because it does, eventually come back), it comes back as bashing damage, which heals much more quickly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T12:30:15-08:00","id":13545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>soul31</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=13530#post13530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not the same - it still slows them down - just a bit less. If someone in the pack is wounded (and don't want to spend essence) for let's say 4 lethal ( which in gmc rules is very propable) the pack still need to wait 1 hour for their brother or sister to fully recover. What about demon cell with someone having on the mend? Around 12 seconds for wounded person and group is ready to go... Let me use more concise wording i meant free instant healing. Or even more precise - free instant aggravated and/or lethal wounds healing. There may be some power that i don't know that heals bashing damage that is free and it's fine. But as on the mend is - it's everyone should have kind of embed now...</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf is partly better as it is never using up an action at all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T13:23:30-08:00","id":13581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=13441#post13441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about this: &quot;The target heals at an acceleraterated rate for a number of hours equal to the demons successes. Recovering one bashing per minute, one lethal every half hour, and one aggravated level every three hours.&quot; That keeps the Embed useful, and true to its original purpose without raining on Break to Heal's parade.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a good one. If the Embed is not changed in the final version, I'm going to use this version instead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T23:12:23-08:00","id":13808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sikker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=13407#post13407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about this: &quot;The target heals at an acceleraterated rate for a number of hours equal to the demons successes. Recovering one bashing per minute, one lethal every half hour, and one aggravated level every three hours.&quot; That keeps the Embed useful, and true to its original purpose without raining on Break to Heal's parade.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like it, however nothing stops demons from having this power always active. This makes it more like a splat property (such as werewolf healing) than a power that is activated and has an effect. What about that version (This would also get rid of the dice rolling):<br /> <br /> Choose one of the following:<br /> - (I) The demon heals the target of all bashing damage,<br /> - (2) The demon heals the target of all lethal damage next time the targets rests. A rest could be a full night sleeping, or half a day in a hospital. The damage vanishes after the target rested at least 10-Stamina hours. A demon could also spend the time in another cover (or demon form), but the damage will remain until the cover she/he took the damage \u00edn finished resting.<br /> - (3) as (2), howver the demon heals (Primum) aggravated damage instead of lethal damage.<br /> Healing a normal human being of aggravated or lethal damage causes a compromise roll, and therefore demons are often loathe to do so.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T00:08:00-08:00","id":13820,"title":"","content":"The odds of a demon accidentally risking cover by having it active all the time are significant, so that is a pretty big discouraging factor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T00:14:28-08:00","id":13823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=13820#post13820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The odds of a demon accidentally risking cover by having it active all the time are significant, so that is a pretty big discouraging factor.</div> </div> </div> </div>But only if a demon uses the power to heal humans. There is no risk healing himself or other demons.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just read your &quot;Spam&quot; houserule; now it makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1125,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","user":"gflash","date":". 11-19-2013, 03:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T02:22:14-08:00","id":13881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gflash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=13823#post13823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But only if a demon uses the power to heal humans. There is no risk healing himself or other demons.<br /> <br /> Edit: Just read your &quot;Spam&quot; houserule; now it makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. If a mortal realizes that the demon got shanked and he's fine an hour late, that would be a compromise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T03:51:58-08:00","id":13918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=13881#post13881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. If a mortal realizes that the demon got shanked and he's fine an hour late, that would be a compromise.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that would mean that virtually any use of On the Mend in a combat situation triggers a compromise. Therefore, shouldn't it be an exploit, since the power is clearly designed to be (also) used in combat?<br /> <br /> It just does'nt fit as an embed in my opinion, because it's not &quot;stealthy&quot; at all. And it's too powerful, no demon in her right mind would go without this embed if she knows about it. Being able to heal even 7 boxes of aggravated damage in less then a minute? Yay!<br /> <br /> The main problem with this power is that it seems not to be optional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T05:20:23-08:00","id":13941,"title":"","content":"Ok then, prometehans - prometheans need to spend two turns plugged to wall socket to heal one point of aggravated damage - it means they got to risk the disquiet (because it make them show their disfigurements for at least 6 turns) - or do this when they're completely alone - it is quite fast healing but it adds to the drama.<br /> <br /> I am not mage specialist how awakened with life 2 can heal without mana expenditure?<br /> <br /> This power also kills the drama which is my opinion very important part of the game. If character in spy movie is hurt and is wanted he got to either steal supplies to heal themselves or find some street doc to help him. This kind of character actually need someone he got to trust - person he got to bribe or blackmail or threaten to make sure this person will not sell them out to the goverment or enemy. Of course, demon got also other option - he can change to the demonic form and risk compromise. See? Choices. Drama. Something that this power kills.<br /> <br /> Also let me ask again - why destroyers have all powers that people are complaining about? They got best defense embed , best healing embed, and best save or die ability. Why guardians don't have on the mend where all his job was - to not let people die they're protecting? Especially if Machine know how people are weak and brittle? There are some not much &quot;balance&quot; issues and more choose this archetype and couple of abilities and see how the theme is going awaaaay just before your eyes - and what we got instead? Hitman or something... Bullet proof, instant healing, guy who defeats everyone just by one punch - it would be so fun playing with someone like that in my group... Where is a horror? Where is a paranoia? Where is spy movie? Where is a drama?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1194-soul31","name":"soul31","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T05:35:23-08:00","id":13945,"title":"","content":"OK, so a bit of insight into my process as a designer: <br /> <br /> 1) I don't get one shit about &quot;game balance.&quot; I think that, in general, when people say &quot;game balance&quot; they're talking &quot;white room combat&quot; and I think that's so far removed from any actual play experience that it's completely useless as part of the process. <br /> <br /> 2) I'm a big fan of killing darlings. If something is assumed to be a rules requirement, I want to know why. If there's something to be gained by fiddling with it, let's fiddle. Sometimes I think it's worth keeping rules principles intact (I was not a fan, for instance, of <b>Mummy</b> having &quot;screw with target number&quot; powers, though I haven't seen that in play so I don't know if it does or doesn't work), but it's always worth examining. <br /> <br /> 3) <i>With that said</i>, I think that a useful definition of &quot;game balance&quot; is, &quot;Is this ability so useful, in the context of the game, that <i>not</i> taking is an objectively dumb idea?&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, I don't think we're quite there yet with On the Mend, and I'll tell you why in a minute. Let's instead look at a power that I think <i>is</i> useful enough that it's unbalanced: Electroshock Recharge from <b>Promethean</b>. It's a level-two Transmutation (so, what, 10XP if you're on Mercurius, 14 if you're not?), and all it does is piggy-back on the Created's existing ability to heal via electrocution; it lets them recharge Pyros as well as Health. In practice, as I've seen running the game, it means that the characters are always fully charged. Now, there are in-setting ways to limit that, but it's still so useful a power that you really should take it; there are few uses of your 10/14XP that give you the same value. If/when we do a revision of <b>Promethean</b> for GMC rules, that's something we'll address.<br /> <br /> For On the Mend, I think we're either at that level or approaching it, but not because it provides free healing. I think that there are two things at work here: first, that it provides free healing <i>for yourself or anyone else, </i>which is pretty potent, and second and more importantly, <i>it works better than an Exploit that does something similar</i>. <br /> <br /> What all that means is that I'm going to revise the Embed somewhat before the final version of the book goes to press. Whatever that revision is, it's not going to be some arbitrary limitation that I put in there to &quot;nerf&quot; the power because it's &quot;too powerful.&quot; It's going to be because I want the power to be consistent - balanced - with the game around it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T06:33:52-08:00","id":13983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=13945#post13945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What all that means is that I'm going to revise the Embed somewhat <b>before the final version of the book goes to press</b>. Whatever that revision is, it's not going to be some arbitrary limitation that I put in there to &quot;nerf&quot; the power because it's &quot;too powerful.&quot; It's going to be because I want the power to be consistent - balanced - with the game around it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry to be as thick as a short plank Matt, but do you mean it will be corrected for the printed version or for the PDF that is being released at the end of this KS? <br /> <br /> Also are there any other Embeds or Exploits you've had feedback on now and are thinking of changing?<br /> <br /> The only one that springs to mind is the Embed - Knockout Punch, which I know some people had issue with (I don't) and even if it remained mechanically the same would you consider giving it a more quantified description e.g. situations where it does not work e.g. against undead. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T07:13:20-08:00","id":14014,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=13945#post13945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and more importantly, <i>it works better than an Exploit that does something similar</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Has there been any consideration given to improving the Exploit, rather then &quot;nerfing&quot; the Embed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/258-thesarcasticsage","name":"TheSarcasticSage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar258_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T08:03:02-08:00","id":14050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheSarcasticSage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=14014#post14014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Has there been any consideration given to improving the Exploit, rather then &quot;nerfing&quot; the Embed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope not. The Embed works at Exploit-level power. It should either be nerfed to fit with the Embed aesthetic or recategorized as an Exploit. Given that powers in Demon are non-linear (except perhaps for Ciphers), flat spell lists, it wouldn't make sense to improve an arbitrary Exploit to handle a problem with an unrelated Embed. <br /> <br /> I think blackhatmatts philosophy of balance as a gauge of internal consistency rather than a gauge of power is sound. I am confident On The Mend will feel more like an Embed once the book hits the press.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T11:06:03-08:00","id":14183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hawthorn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=13983#post13983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to be as thick as a short plank Matt, but do you mean it will be corrected for the printed version or for the PDF that is being released at the end of this KS?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he means for the PDF; that is, after all, being released for sale, which is what &quot;going to press&quot; typically means in this circumstance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T01:29:22-08:00","id":14587,"title":"","content":"Well Mages are the only ones who can stack armour, and I haven't seen much complaints about that.<br /> <br /> Cross-template &quot;balance&quot; shouldn't be too much of a debate. I agree with Matt here about people obsessing about white room numbers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T05:21:31-08:00","id":14658,"title":"","content":"And Mage Armor might well change when we update <b>Mage</b> to GMC rules, anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think that I'm more likely to tone down On the Mend than beef up Break to Heal (fun fact: the first draft version of that power was called &quot;Break Shit, Heal Buddy&quot;). <br /> <br /> And yeah, any changes we make will be in the for-sale version of the book, in whatever format. I suppose &quot;goes to press&quot; is somewhat of an outdated expression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T06:20:52-08:00","id":14668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=14658#post14658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Mage Armor might well change when we update <b>Mage</b> to GMC rules, anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I think that I'm more likely to tone down On the Mend than beef up Break to Heal (fun fact: the first draft version of that power was called &quot;Break Shit, Heal Buddy&quot;).<br /> <br /> And yeah, any changes we make will be in the for-sale version of the book, in whatever format. I suppose &quot;goes to press&quot; is somewhat of an outdated expression.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> YES Matt YES! Although that kinda goes against what I said above, this is the moment I dreamt of.<br /> <br /> Wonderful.<br /> <br /> [edit] about Mage Armour, that is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T16:44:25-08:00","id":14965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=13945#post13945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, so a bit of insight into my process as a designer:<br /> <br /> 1) I don't get one shit about &quot;game balance.&quot; I think that, in general, when people say &quot;game balance&quot; they're talking &quot;white room combat&quot; and I think that's so far removed from any actual play experience that it's completely useless as part of the process.<br /> <br /> 2) I'm a big fan of killing darlings. If something is assumed to be a rules requirement, I want to know why. If there's something to be gained by fiddling with it, let's fiddle. Sometimes I think it's worth keeping rules principles intact (I was not a fan, for instance, of <b>Mummy</b> having &quot;screw with target number&quot; powers, though I haven't seen that in play so I don't know if it does or doesn't work), but it's always worth examining.<br /> <br /> 3) <i>With that said</i>, I think that a useful definition of &quot;game balance&quot; is, &quot;Is this ability so useful, in the context of the game, that <i>not</i> taking is an objectively dumb idea?&quot;<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> What all that means is that I'm going to revise the Embed somewhat before the final version of the book goes to press. Whatever that revision is, it's not going to be some arbitrary limitation that I put in there to &quot;nerf&quot; the power because it's &quot;too powerful.&quot; It's going to be because I want the power to be consistent - balanced - with the game around it.</div> </div> </div> </div>When people say &quot;I don't care about game balance&quot;, what I, at least, tend to hear (can't speak for other people, but I assume I'm not literally the only one) is &quot;I expect the GM to work extra hard in order to make this game fun rather than think things through&quot;. A surprisingly common position, online! I must say, I was quite apprehensive about what effects this lack of balance might have on <i>Demon</i>.<br /> <br /> Good to see you believe in most of the useful design principles behind &quot;balance&quot;, but not the stupid stuff that gets attached to the word.<br /> <br /> I must say, perhaps we should all start giving our own definitions of &quot;balance&quot; rather than, as seems increasingly common, talking past each other <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> the term means all things to all men, it seems sometimes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 11-20-2013, 07:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T19:05:51-08:00","id":15046,"title":"","content":"&quot;White Room&quot; balance is useless as an exercise, as it tends to ignore many significant factors in order to test a situation that basically doesn't exist in game: two characters enter and fight to the death for no reason, unaided and under equipped. It's a fairly dumb premise that produces dumb results. It's especially bad when we are doing this across game lines; that's like asking if a 7th level Tiefling Warlock/Fighter can beat an Adeptes Astartes Space Marine - it's just a pointless comparison. Such things can be fun exercises but ultimately shouldn't be used as any kind of game evaluation tool.<br /> <br /> What does matter are apple to apple comparisons, such as when a low level power does the exact same schtick as a higher level power, or very close comparisons can be made, such as with say, damage output. There it is a matter of making all available choices valid, and that's the most important thing in RPGs. You must be able to make choices and those choices must be valid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T01:51:28-08:00","id":15245,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I was not so much concerned because the power was OP (though it did flirt with the point where anyone who expected to get into a fight should really take it), but because there was another healing power, one that is supposed to have an extra oomph at the price of attracting attention, yet this Exploit was objectively inferior to the Embed, to the point nobody in their right mind should take it if they could take the Embed instead. And that just bugs me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T18:48:50-08:00","id":26889,"title":"","content":"While it's a good ability, I don't actually have a problem with it, and here's why: I don't think that it fails Matt's &quot;Is this ability so useful, <b><i>in the context of the game</i></b>&quot; test. Consider this:<br /> <br /> 1) Changing into their demonic form shouldn't really be a standard tactic, given the myriad of risks associated with doing so. The consequences of any kind of detection of your true form in Demon is <i>vastly </i>greater than for the other supernaturals, so I would expect that tactic to be much rarer than it is in other games;<br /> <br /> 2) As a result of (1), the vast majority of combat will probably be engaged in without breaking Cover unless it's really, really necessary;<br /> <br /> 3) When in Cover, Demons are squishy. Really squishy. As squishy as any bog-standard human;<br /> <br /> 4) As a result of the above, I would expect most Demons to avoid combat unless it's completely unavoidable. This is, first and foremost, a 'spy' game. In that context, if bullets start to fly then 99% of the time it's because you've already failed and you're at your backup or bug-out plan. This is not a game where combat should be the first (or even second) solution to your problems. Hell, just unwanted attention by human law enforcement is enough to cause demons all sorts of problems that other supernaturals just don't have to worry about (or at least, not as much);<br /> <br /> 5) Therefore, while a nice ability, I wouldn't expect it to see as much use in <b>actual play</b> as it would in other games, which intrinsicly reduces its value;<br /> <br /> 6) By taking it (or any other combat power, many of which are also very nice) you are <i>denying </i>yourself access to an alternate power. Many of those other powers have widespread applicability and are, frankly, so full of utility in your day-to-day operations that it's just not funny.<br /> <br /> Seriously, just looking at some of the other Cacophany embeds, if you can't figure out a way to use Cause and Effect, Left or Right?, Lucky Break or Sabotage to great effect in combat, you're not thinking hard enough. Plus, all of those have great utility in normal activities as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1606-psychochink","name":"Psychochink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T23:52:51-08:00","id":27033,"title":"","content":"I suspect you'd see a lot more people grabbing Just Bruised as their combat survival tactic and have someone in the group use On the Mend after a few rounds of 1 damage piles up.<br /> <br /> The riskier (but far cooler in my eyes) option would be Just Bruised + Momentum to take the successes on the attacker's roll and use those to buff your Just Bruised roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T09:45:30-08:00","id":27267,"title":"","content":"My issue with &quot;On the Mend&quot; is the calculations for healing lethal and aggravated damage. As the Demon gains more ranks in primum he will heal agg damage easier than lethal. I'd change the healing of lethal to successes rolled, or primum whichever is higher, and successes rolled or primum whichever is lower for aggravated damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I'm immortal, I've been right so far&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/301-bwchism","name":"bwchism","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar301_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T11:39:22-08:00","id":27348,"title":"","content":"This has been super informative. Thank you Matt <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> &quot;Electroshock Recharge&quot; is like, the poster-child in my mind for &quot;take this shit.&quot; I tell new PCs about it whenever Promethean comes up; it's a no-brainer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T05:39:16-08:00","id":27917,"title":"","content":"Well, if we do a GMC update to Promethean next year, it'll probably just come standard. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T07:00:47-08:00","id":27948,"title":"","content":"Matt, would you mind previewing the corrected rules on this thread pre-pdf launch (in the event that the KS pdf does not come out this month)? Some of us are already playing and this would be very helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T09:19:05-08:00","id":28033,"title":"","content":"I don't have a problem with Demons healing themselves stupid easily. It's in theme for them. Healing others though, that sounds more like Pact material to me. Lying on the ground bleeding out, or in bed dying of cancer or whatever? Those are easy targets to get a soul from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T11:48:15-08:00","id":28158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JoeB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=27948#post27948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matt, would you mind previewing the corrected rules on this thread pre-pdf launch (in the event that the KS pdf does not come out this month)? Some of us are already playing and this would be very helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sure. Here ya go:<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Success: </b>Choose one: All of the target's bashing damage heals in fifteen minutes, <i>or</i> all of the target's lethal damage heals overnight, <i>or</i> all of the target's aggravated damage changes to lethal. A given target can only benefit from one use of On the Mend at a time, meaning that if the demon uses the Embed to change aggravated damage to lethal, she cannot then use the Embed to speed the target's healing of the lethal damage. Healing a normal human being of aggravated or lethal <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\">damage causes a compromise roll, and therefore demons are </span>often loathe to do so. The demon can use this Embed on herself.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><b>Exceptional Success: </b>As above, except the options are as </span>follows: Target heals all bashing damage<span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\">; target heals all lethal damage in an hour; </span>target heals one point of aggravated damage per success or per dot of the demon\u2019s Primum, whichever is lower.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T12:02:28-08:00","id":28172,"title":"","content":"The Exception Success is a touch weird as it appears to heal Aggravated damage <u>faster</u> than lethal. Might I suggest:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><b>Exceptional Success: </b>As above, except the options are as </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">follows: Target immediately heals all bashing damage</span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\">; target heals all lethal damage in an hour; </span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">target downgrades all aggravated damage to bashing. </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 12-11-2013, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T18:35:35-08:00","id":28441,"title":"","content":"While it might appear to do so, it looks to me like you'd need to get 6 successes <i>and</i> 6 Primum to heal aggravated the way you heal lethal with an ES (5 of each if your target has Stamina of 1 or is a teenager). Otherwise, you'd probably heal 1-4, <i>possibly</i> 5 if your Primum is that high. You'd still be in the danger zone, and you'd still have a <i>lot</i> of aggravated damage to heal. Aggravated damage that wouldn't benefit from another use of On the Mend.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T18:44:43-08:00","id":28443,"title":"","content":"I like the change. Actually makes it even more useful to a character who's the one who patches their Ring up after trouble (like one I'm currently playing, or at least that's the intent) while leaving Break to Mend desirable as the 'back on their feet NOW!' power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T23:40:28-08:00","id":28565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=28158#post28158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, sure. Here ya go:</div> </div> </div> </div>These changes are great, I really like them. Thanks a lot!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1125-gflash","name":"gflash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1125_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T00:21:21-08:00","id":28572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Grim Lich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=28441#post28441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it might appear to do so, it looks to me like you'd need to get 6 successes <i>and</i> 6 Primum to heal aggravated the way you heal lethal with an ES (5 of each if your target has Stamina of 1 or is a teenager). Otherwise, you'd probably heal 1-4, <i>possibly</i> 5 if your Primum is that high. You'd still be in the danger zone, and you'd still have a <i>lot</i> of aggravated damage to heal. Aggravated damage that wouldn't benefit from another use of On the Mend.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the contrary, lets say you've got a character with Primum 3. He's taken 4 damage. If this damage is aggravated an exceptional success immediately heals 3 points of it, leaving him with 1 Agg. Since he's no longer benefiting from accelerated healing at this point he could then immediately activate it a second time and heal that agg at lethal speed (or faster, if he's very lucky). If that damage is lethal he gains no immediate benefit, and ties up further use of On the Mend for the next hour. One hour later he's in peak condition, but that doesn't help if he's already dead. <br /> <br /> In other words, in the thick of battle (where quick healing really counts) he'd be in better shape if he'd taken aggravated damage than if he'd taken lethal. It's niche, but weirdly counter-intuitive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T01:16:26-08:00","id":28591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=28158#post28158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">A given target can only benefit from one use of On the Mend at a time, meaning that if the demon uses the Embed to change aggravated damage to lethal, she cannot then use the Embed to speed the target's healing of the lethal damage.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is pretty clear. You can only use it on any one set of wounds. Now, if you get struck for aggravated damage again the next round, you can use it again on that, but you can't use the Embed on aggravated damage that you took before you last used the Embed.<br /> <br /> It's like if you have a target from whom you remove aggravated damage. Let's say they've taken 5 points of aggravated damage \u2014 the werewolf's claws just ripped through your buddy's cover body like it was tissue paper. So you use On the Mend, and your buddy heals 3 points (we'll go with your Primum 3 example). Presto, 3 aggravated are healed. His lungs are no longer in tatters, but there's still deep gouges in his flesh and his right arm is still suffering from a compound fracture. You can't use On the Mend to heal it again; you already used On the Mend to patch up what you could using that particular Embed.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, you might have to worry about yourself; that werewolf and his friends now know that you can fix up major wounds. They're probably going to try and take you out ASAP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":1122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","user":"The Grim Lich","date":". 12-12-2013, 04:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T01:53:15-08:00","id":28595,"title":"","content":"I think the conflict is coming from differences in interpretation. I read &quot;A given target can only benefit from one use of On the Mend at a time&quot; to mean that, once they've set to healing they can't use the Embed again until <b>all the wounds affected by On the Mend are healed. </b> That's a pretty clear line when dealing with bashing and lethal, you wait until the character has recovered all the damage taken at the time they used the Embed. But for something like an Exceptional Success on agg, where the Embed does all it's work in one action, it's less clear cut.<br /> <br /> Correct me if I'm wrong, you seem to be reading it as &quot;once the demon has used On the Mend he cannot use it on himself again until he's completely healed.&quot; Which I'll admit is what I'd prefer it does (with the kicker that it can't be spammed on the same person more than once in a scene).<br /> <br /> Even then what would you say to the situation where the Werewolf did 3 Agg, and the Demon heals himself completely? Would you rule that the Demon still has to wait? Or that, having healed all damage, he can now use On the Mend on himself again.<br /> <br /> Note: I like this version, it's just a little weird and ambiguous.<br /> <br /> Edit: Actually, my original point still stands. If the Werewolf in your example had dealt Lethal damage the demon would still have 5 lethal boxes filled, putting him ~2-4 damage away from bleeding to death. But because it did Aggravated damage he has 3 more health worth of buffer, meaning the Werewolf has to do ~5 - 7 damage before the demon dies. In this life-or-death situation, having taken aggravated damage improved his chances of survival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 12-12-2013, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T05:44:24-08:00","id":28657,"title":"","content":"Perhaps a timeframe was intended to be added to the Agg heal, too.<br /> Then again, that might be intentional. Aggravated damage is usually from something 'unnatural', and one of the quirks of Demons is that they resist the weird stuff a lot better than plain old pointy things. Though this gets muddled because Aggravated represents mere overflow damage, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T05:46:50-08:00","id":28658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=28158#post28158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, sure. Here ya go:<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Success: </b>Choose one: All of the target's bashing damage heals in fifteen minutes, <i>or</i> all of the target's lethal damage heals overnight, <i>or</i> all of the target's aggravated damage changes to lethal. A given target can only benefit from one use of On the Mend at a time, meaning that if the demon uses the Embed to change aggravated damage to lethal, she cannot then use the Embed to speed the target's healing of the lethal damage. Healing a normal human being of aggravated or lethal <span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\">damage causes a compromise roll, and therefore demons are </span>often loathe to do so. The demon can use this Embed on herself.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\"><b>Exceptional Success: </b>As above, except the options are as </span>follows: Target heals all bashing damage<span style=\"font-family:arial, sans-serif\">; target heals all lethal damage in an hour; </span>target heals one point of aggravated damage per success or per dot of the demon\u2019s Primum, whichever is lower.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Super awesome, thanks Matt!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T05:50:24-08:00","id":28660,"title":"","content":"Something to consider, too: It's a hell of lot easier to take lethal damage than agg. There are very few sources of straight-up agg damage in the World of Darkness, and none that are specific to demons (that is, they don't have a silver analog). As such, from a game play perspective, I'm OK with high-Primum demons healing agg damage faster, because they're supernaturally more powerful anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T11:16:45-08:00","id":28826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=28595#post28595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correct me if I'm wrong, you seem to be reading it as &quot;once the demon has used On the Mend he cannot use it on himself again until he's completely healed.&quot; Which I'll admit is what I'd prefer it does (with the kicker that it can't be spammed on the same person more than once in a scene).<br /> <br /> Even then what would you say to the situation where the Werewolf did 3 Agg, and the Demon heals himself completely? Would you rule that the Demon still has to wait? Or that, having healed all damage, he can now use On the Mend on himself again.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reading is that OTM can be used once per &quot;damage from attack&quot;. In the example above, I was assuming that the Werewolf was using the gift that causes them to grow claws that deal Agg damage straight up to pretty much anything. In your example, I'd say sure, he could use OTM again as soon as he takes more damage \u2014 although given how he's in combat, using OTM more than once or twice would <i>probably</i> call for a compromise roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T13:47:48-08:00","id":28906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Grim Lich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=28826#post28826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> My reading is that OTM can be used once per &quot;damage from attack&quot;. In the example above, I was assuming that the Werewolf was using the gift that causes them to grow claws that deal Agg damage straight up to pretty much anything. In your example, I'd say sure, he could use OTM again as soon as he takes more damage \u2014 although given how he's in combat, using OTM more than once or twice would <i>probably</i> call for a compromise roll.</div> </div> </div> </div> That makes sense logically, but it does mean you have to do some awkward bookkeeping. Under this interpretation, If there's anyone in the group with on the mend, you have to keep track of what damage came from what attacks so you know how many uses of On the Mend you can use on someone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T15:08:42-08:00","id":28956,"title":"","content":"I think there's a bit of 'squeaky wheel' going on here, as well as forgetting the context of the game. Remember guys, this and Break to Heal are the <i>only </i>healing powers in the game - and not every (or even most) characters are going to have either. There's no innate healing (other than changing to demon form, and that's not a lot). Demons are squishy enough as it is, let's not go overboard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1606-psychochink","name":"Psychochink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T16:25:14-08:00","id":28987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psychochink</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=28956#post28956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's a bit of 'squeaky wheel' going on here, as well as forgetting the context of the game. Remember guys, this and Break to Heal are the <i>only </i>healing powers in the game - and not every (or even most) characters are going to have either. There's no innate healing (other than changing to demon form, and that's not a lot). Demons are squishy enough as it is, let's not go overboard.</div> </div> </div> </div> The complete lack of other healing options is actually a big part of why On the Mend was a &quot;you'd be an idiot not to take this&quot; power. If there were lots of healing powers of its caliber, it would just be one useful power among many. Being both the only option and a very powerful one makes it suboptimal to pass up. That said, I think the proposed changes pretty much fix the issue of On the Mend being better than Break to Heal, which is the only thing I was really concerned with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T17:29:10-08:00","id":29024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=28906#post28906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That makes sense logically, but it does mean you have to do some awkward bookkeeping. Under this interpretation, If there's anyone in the group with on the mend, you have to keep track of what damage came from what attacks so you know how many uses of On the Mend you can use on someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>All magical healing in Shadowrun works that way, so it's not exactly an unprecedented system.<br /> <br /> I will probably treat it like I do in Shadowrun for my own sanity's sake, bookkeeping-wise: applying Heal disqualifies someone from receiving it until they get hurt again. This does lead to the occasional scenario where a character (usually the group's Fridge Troll, who is built to survive this kind of thing) gets a giant flesh taco carved out of their abdomen, gets a healing spell from one of the group's casters, takes a tiny little bit of damage from someone trying to shoot them with a pistol, and then the next healing spell is working on taco damage too. It's much more likely that by the time the healer's turn comes around again, there will be another taco to deal with.<br /> <br /> And there are already other effects that imply a need to track individual wounds in Demon, like Shift Consequences. ...okay, maybe that's the only other one. Still, they're there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T17:31:54-08:00","id":29027,"title":"","content":"There's loads of damage preventing powers though, like Just Bruised. Also if they have the Wound Healing Demonic Form power, they could just partially manifest that as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T18:00:18-08:00","id":29037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pgolasze13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=29027#post29027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's loads of damage preventing powers though, like Just Bruised. Also if they have the Wound Healing Demonic Form power, they could just partially manifest that as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if there's any candidate for a 'this really should be standard' form power, it's that, but I'm not sure it's needed with everything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1096-squidheadjax","name":"squidheadjax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1096_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T19:03:29-08:00","id":29080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>squidheadjax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=29037#post29037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, if there's any candidate for a 'this really should be standard' form power, it's that, but I'm not sure it's needed with everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or maybe downgrade it to a Modification or a Technology - that way it's still optional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1606-psychochink","name":"Psychochink","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T04:53:40-08:00","id":29248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=28987#post28987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The complete lack of other healing options is actually a big part of why On the Mend was a &quot;you'd be an idiot not to take this&quot; power. If there were lots of healing powers of its caliber, it would just be one useful power among many. Being both the only option and a very powerful one makes it suboptimal to pass up. That said, I think the proposed changes pretty much fix the issue of On the Mend being better than Break to Heal, which is the only thing I was really concerned with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose my playtest group was full of idiots, then, as not a single one of them took the power. Instead, they simply stayed the hell out of combat as much as possible. Actually, I have to give them a hell of a lot of credit - my group played up their Covers very well and avoided doing much of anything to compromise them. I tried to get them into combat a few times (I mean, we were testing the system, after all), but it only actually worked once.<br /> <br /> Now, if a ring is getting into a lot of combat, then sure On the Mend is incredibly useful. If not, then it isn't so much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T08:06:51-08:00","id":29316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>strider1276</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=29248#post29248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I suppose my playtest group was full of idiots, then, as not a single one of them took the power. Instead, they simply stayed the hell out of combat as much as possible. Actually, I have to give them a hell of a lot of credit - my group played up their Covers very well and avoided doing much of anything to compromise them. I tried to get them into combat a few times (I mean, we were testing the system, after all), but it only actually worked once. Now, if a ring is getting into a lot of combat, then sure On the Mend is incredibly useful. If not, then it isn't so much.</div> </div> </div> </div> Apologies, I was being hyperbolic. Of course, any healing power will only be useful if combat is a common enough occurrence that you won't usually heal naturally before the next time combat happens. But if you expect much combat, it is a bit of an auto-take power. Again, not so much because of its power, but because healing options are pretty limited. Honestly though, I didn't see a problem with the power, other than it being better than Break to Heal in most situations you'd want it. But that's been fixed, so I think we're pretty much good here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T14:36:47-08:00","id":29532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=29316#post29316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Apologies, I was being hyperbolic. Of course, any healing power will only be useful if combat is a common enough occurrence that you won't usually heal naturally before the next time combat happens. But if you expect much combat, it is a bit of an auto-take power. Again, not so much because of its power, but because healing options are pretty limited. Honestly though, I didn't see a problem with the power, other than it being better than Break to Heal in most situations you'd want it. But that's been fixed, so I think we're pretty much good here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, that's fine - my apologies if I came across a bit harsh, as that wasn't my intent whatsoever. But yeah, since it's getting fixed, no big deal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T01:28:18-08:00","id":30330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=28158#post28158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, sure. Here ya go:<br /> <b>Success: </b>Choose one: All of the target's bashing damage heals in fifteen minutes, <i>or</i> <b><u>all of the target's lethal damage heals overnight,</u></b> <i>or</i> all of the target's aggravated damage changes to lethal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure of the usefulness of this for lethal damage. Overnight would be, what, 6-8 hours of rest? Normal healing of 1 Lethal per hour would have that heal 6-8 Lethal, or more health boxes than anyone without Stamina of 4+.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":1642,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","user":"Paddon","date":". 12-15-2013, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T02:09:03-08:00","id":30339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paddon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=30330#post30330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure of the usefulness of this for lethal damage. Overnight would be, what, 6-8 hours of rest? Normal healing of 1 Lethal per hour would have that heal 6-8 Lethal, or more health boxes than anyone without Stamina of 4+.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are you getting 1 Lethal per hour from? Core book says 1 point every two days (WoD:Core pg. 175)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T08:00:52-08:00","id":30421,"title":"","content":"it's one lethal per hour if your a werewolf, but that's it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T08:55:51-08:00","id":30447,"title":"","content":"Personally, for an embed I'd have gone with something more along the lines of an &quot;It's only a flesh wound&quot; sort of power. <br /> A&gt; Has to be used on the target <b>before</b> any one with medical training looks at them and assess the real extent of the damage.<br /> B&gt; Can reduce any amount of Bashing damage to 1 bashing total<br /> C&gt; OR can downgrade any amount of Lethal to 1 Lethal and the rest Bashing<br /> D&gt; OR can downgrade Primum Aggravated damage to Lethal, but must leave at least 1 Agg<br /> <br /> The idea being, a Gunshot is never going to NOT be a gunshot, but in the heat of battle can you really know if it was a through-and-through in the fleshy part of the arm or if the bullet struck the shoulder joint? Not without taking a few moments to examine the wound. Yes, Bob got caught in the edge of the car exploding, and yes, he is Burned (aggravated Damage) but how badly? You don't know. People get struck by Lightning every year. Some of them die instantly, cooked and frazzled, but every so often someone lives, sometimes spending as little as 3 months recovering. If you're skydiving and your chute (and back up chute) fail, well, hitting the ground at terminal velocity also tends to be an insta-kill scenario, with most of the bones in your body shattered. Except there are documented cases of people literally getting up and walking (well, hobbling) away from such a fall, with minor fractures but no breaks. 13000 feet into the ground resulting in what, in game terms, might be 2 lethal and the rest of the bar bruised.<br /> <br /> I'd build the healing power off the same quantum uncertainty that fuels things like In My Pocket. Everyone involved <b>knows</b> the target is injured, hence the power can't remove all injury, but unless or until someone with some real medical skill examines the wounded person you don't <b>really</b> know how badly they're hurt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T10:25:02-08:00","id":30478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=30447#post30447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, for an embed I'd have gone with something more along the lines of an &quot;It's only a flesh wound&quot; sort of power. A&gt; Has to be used on the target <b>before</b> any one with medical training looks at them and assess the real extent of the damage. B&gt; Can reduce any amount of Bashing damage to 1 bashing total C&gt; OR can downgrade any amount of Lethal to 1 Lethal and the rest Bashing D&gt; OR can downgrade Primum Aggravated damage to Lethal, but must leave at least 1 Agg The idea being, a Gunshot is never going to NOT be a gunshot, but in the heat of battle can you really know if it was a through-and-through in the fleshy part of the arm or if the bullet struck the shoulder joint? Not without taking a few moments to examine the wound. Yes, Bob got caught in the edge of the car exploding, and yes, he is Burned (aggravated Damage) but how badly? You don't know. People get struck by Lightning every year. Some of them die instantly, cooked and frazzled, but every so often someone lives, sometimes spending as little as 3 months recovering. If you're skydiving and your chute (and back up chute) fail, well, hitting the ground at terminal velocity also tends to be an insta-kill scenario, with most of the bones in your body shattered. Except there are documented cases of people literally getting up and walking (well, hobbling) away from such a fall, with minor fractures but no breaks. 13000 feet into the ground resulting in what, in game terms, might be 2 lethal and the rest of the bar bruised. I'd build the healing power off the same quantum uncertainty that fuels things like In My Pocket. Everyone involved <b>knows</b> the target is injured, hence the power can't remove all injury, but unless or until someone with some real medical skill examines the wounded person you don't <b>really</b> know how badly they're hurt.</div> </div> </div> </div> You could easily narrate On the Mend to work that way in the story without having to change the mechanics. But a power that reduces the extent of damage already exists, I'd be worried about stealing Just Bruised's thunder. Plus it's nice to have a legit healing power if you ask me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T11:10:48-08:00","id":30492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13377-demon-got-free-healing?p=30339#post30339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where are you getting 1 Lethal per hour from? Core book says 1 point every two days (WoD:Core pg. 175)</div> </div> </div> </div>You're absolutely right, I had an incredible brainfart. That's what happens when one is RPG-deprived.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Once is happenstance. Twice is coincidence. Three times is enemy action. Four times is Infrastructure.<br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> Rule #2: Never let the game-mechanics get in the way of a good story.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1642-paddon","name":"Paddon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T11:15:28-08:00","id":30494,"title":"","content":"I had completely forgotten about Just Bruised. Or more accurately, since I've been reading several game books, I thought it was a power from Adventure!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T01:55:45-08:00","id":50530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Embeds are supposed to be powers similar to what demons used as angels, and the mightiest angel serving the God-Machine only gets the Regenerate Numen to heal himself, which only slowly heals bashing and lethal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do yourself a favor and <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/embedscanbenumina.png\" target=\"_blank\">look at what the Lambent's Numina include</a>.<br /> <br /> It's a really bad idea to argue from upper bounds on powers that explicitly can draw from PC powersets in addition to not strictly <i>having</i> upper bounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 01-16-2014, 04:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-16T10:05:10-08:00","id":50801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tau Neutrino</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's circular reasoning.</div> </div> </div> </div>No more than your argument that the powers explicitly based on angelic Numina and Influences can't be replicated by angelic Numina and Influences because the powers that work by overcharging the same principles are outside the scope of angelic obedience to use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lambent sounds like shorthand for describing the effect of a new Numina, like way mages get described with Gifts and Rites in the Werewolf book. </div> </div> </div><i>That is my goddamn <b>point.</b></i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Brilliant, a Rank 3 hunter angel, has Regenerate, as does the Rank 4 Y2K angel. If they could use a power that makes Regenerate obsolete, why don't they? </div> </div> </div>Because On The Mend is a patch-up trick and angels are a) purpose-built, b) immortal, and c) capable of receiving maintenance. An angel with a job for which On The Mend would be <i>relevant</i> would be as likely to have it as the rare angel made with Resurrection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}